Important naming clarification

In these sprite filenames:

* ba means basic attack
* 1ba means Basic Attack 1
* therefore the existing internal action1 input is the input for BA1
* the number at the very end of a filename is the animation frame number

Examples:

* 0001_1ba1.png = Basic Attack 1, frame 1
* 0001_1ba4.png = Basic Attack 1, frame 4
* 0001_midair1ba3.png = mid-air Basic Attack 1, frame 3

Do not interpret 1ba1 as attack 1BA1 or create a new unrelated action.

Keep the existing internal input name action1; do not rename the whole input system. Only change its user-facing meaning/label to Basic Attack 1 / BA1 where appropriate.

Existing repo architecture to preserve

The game is already structured correctly for this:

* js/data/characters.js owns character animations, action mappings, attack definitions, movement, hurtboxes, etc.
* js/game/character.js owns the Fighter state machine and tryAction().
* js/game/combat.js already provides startup/active/recovery, damage, hitboxes, knockback, hitstun, blockstun, hitstop and cooldowns.
* js/game/sprite-normalizer.js normalizes different sprite scales and anchors them bottom-centre.
* js/game/sprite-animator.js handles non-looping clips and fallback animations.
* js/core/app.js preloads every path returned by characterFramePaths().
* action1 is already wired through keyboard, touch and gamepad.
* U is the keyboard binding for action1.
* standard gamepad B / Circle is already mapped to action1.
* the training CPU must remain non-attacking.
* Primary, Special and Action 2 must remain reserved/inactive unless they already have real artwork. Do not make up attacks for them.

Follow the same approach used by PR #15 when jump/fall/land were added: real artwork only, canonical character asset folder, data-driven definitions, graceful missing-frame behavior, tests, and no physics/collider changes merely to accommodate artwork.

