3. Ground hurt versus mid-air hurt

The Fighter’s logical combat state should remain hitstun; do not unnecessarily rename the entire combat concept.

Instead, choose the rendered animation based on whether the fighter is grounded while in hitstun:

* hitstun + grounded → hurt
* hitstun + airborne → midairHurt

hitstun must continue having higher visual priority than attack, land, run, jump, fall, block, crouch and idle, consistent with the current state ordering.

If an airborne fighter lands while hitstun is still active, switching from the mid-air hurt art to the grounded hurt art is acceptable and desirable.

When hitstun expires, normal state selection should resume naturally:

* idle/run when grounded
* jump/fall when airborne
* etc.

Do not change movement physics, collider sizes, pushbox sizes, normal hurtboxes, gravity, jump velocity, stage collision or camera behavior just to display the hurt frames.

